{
  "about": "Settings (DESIGN 5.17), kept per person as JSON on their machine. A kept value is taken back only when it still fits its setting; one that does not (a setting removed, an enum value gone, a number past its `min` or `max`, a value of another type) is dropped, and the setting has its default. `fits` gives whether a kept value fits a setting: its type (`text`, `email`, `url`, `color`, `integer`, `duration`, `decimal`, `money`, `bool`, `date`, `datetime`, `enum` with its `values`, `language` with the project's `languages`, `theme` with the offered `themes`), and `min` and `max` for numbers. Decimals and money are kept as text, so they stay exact; dates as `2026-10-23`, moments as `2026-10-23T14:30:00`. `kept` gives the settings a start takes from what was kept: only the settings there are, and only values that fit. `file` gives where an application keeps them, for its system (`windows`, `macos`, or another, `linux`) and its environment: in the folder for application settings (`APPDATA` on Windows; `Library/Application Support` in `HOME` on macOS; `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, else `.config` in `HOME`, elsewhere), in a folder of the program's name, as `settings.json`; nowhere (null) when the environment names no such folder. Paths are written with `/`.",
